      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For beam deflection calculations, you'll primarily need the beam's span length, the beam's cross-sectional dimensions (depth and width), and the material's properties, specifically the Modulus of Elasticity ($E$) for Douglas Fir. You'll use the appropriate beam deflection formulas, which depend on how the beam is supported (e.g., simply supported or fixed). Always consult local building codes and an engineer to ensure your design meets safety and serviceability requirements.",
