    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay thanks. the span is gonna be 14 feet. i'm thinking of using a 6x12 for the beam. i'm also worried about any hidden stuff in the wood itself, like internal knots or grain issues that i might not see easily. how much do those kinds of interior defects impact the load capacity or the risk of sudden failure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Interior defects like large knots or poor grain patterns can significantly reduce the effective strength of a timber beam, potentially leading to premature failure under load. These flaws introduce stress concentrations, meaning the load won't be distributed evenly across the wood fibers. To mitigate this, use lumber rated for structural use and specify clear or select grades from your supplier.",
      "source": "target",
